      walkthrough = "**Status: Incomplete**\n\nQuest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Maiden's Eye [ToL]\n**Who:**\n- Senshali Sa Sivuela [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 115\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 24:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 00:15:00\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Centian Xi Datiar [npc=56862]\n- Diabo Sivuela [ _Quests_]\n- a newly freed slave [npc=56863]\n- a patrolling scout [npc=57167]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Partisan of Maiden's Eye (10 Points) [quest=10570]\n**Era:** | !Terror of Luclin\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Oct 14 18:11:46 2021\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Terror of Luclin Info & Guides: Overview \\| Progression & Task List \\| Raiding \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\nThis is a shared task.\nSenshali Sa Sivuela [npc=56888] is located in the northwest part of Maiden's Eye, near a rock. She is on the find tool CTRL F.\nYou say, 'Hail, Senshali Sa Sivuela'\nSenshali Sa Sivuela appears completely unfazed by your presence, 'As the mistress foretold, you have arrived at this moment to assist us, mortal.' Senshali Sa Sivuela points in a direction. 'It would benefit both factions if you visited the refugee camp to the southeast. I do not know what is drawing all of you here, but I implore you to speak with our leader, [Diabo Sivuela]. He has been awaiting your return to Luclin.'\nYou say, 'Where can I find Diabo Sivuela?'\nSenshali Sa Sivuela says, 'Diabo Sivuela can be found under the tent, in the camp to the southeast. Please speak with him immediately, I believe he has a task of great import that will need your expertise.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Threading the Loop'.\nUpon returning to the Maiden's Eye, Senshali Sa Sivuela has requested that you speak with Diabo Sivuela in the camp to the southeast. It appears that he may have a task that could use your skills.\n\n---\n\n**1\\. Introduce yourself to Diabo Sivuela 0/1 Maiden's Eye**\nThe akhevan camp is found to the southeast. Speak with the camp leader, Diabo Sivuela.\nDiabo Sivuela [npc=56900] is located in the akhevan camp in the southeast corner of the zone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Diabo Sivuela'\nDiabo Sivuela glares at you with a stern, uneasy look. 'We have divined your return to the Maiden's Eye, but your intentions are unknown to us. As you can see, this camp is the home to refugees from both Ka Vethan and the outpost to the north. Not all of us agree with the tenets of our laws. That is why this [camp] exists.'\nYou say, 'What can you tell me about this camp?'\nDiabo Sivuela says, 'This camp is home to those who wish to be free of the oppression of my people, as well as those who escaped Ka Vethan before utter destruction. The akheva in this camp are rebels who fled Ka Vethan in order to survive. Ka Vethan has been rebuilt, and there is some difference of opinion as to how the Maiden of Whispers wants the moon to be preserved. Many of our kind believe that only us akheva should benefit from the moon's grace. We, on the other hand, believe something [different].'\nYou say, 'different'\nDiabo Sivuela says, 'We think what our people have been doing to the gorongans and the vampyre is an insult to Luclin. She has blessed them, and yourselves it seems, with passage into her domain. Yet my kin believe they are more deserving of this domain and wish to use their power and strength to subjugate anyone who does not follow their same beliefs. This camp is meant to be a haven for those who wish to be freed. Will you help us with this endeavor? Will you [help] the resistance?'\nYou say, 'How can we help?'\nDiabo Sivuela says, 'It just so happens that we have a task uniquely suited to your talents. We have arranged a jailbreak of sorts. To the north of here you will find a house. That house holds the strongest of the workers. The slave masters believe that if you want others to work hard, show them a carrot and then beat them with a stick. The slaves who reside there have already been completely indoctrinated and are willing to kill and die for their masters. I warn you to stay away from that building. However, there is a meeting point to the east next to three large trees. You will be able to find one of our agents there ready to escort some newly freed slaves. Meet with them for further instructions.'\nYour task 'Threading the Loop' has been updated.\n**2\\. Meet with Diabo Sivuela's associate to the north 0/1 Maiden's Eye**\nFind the agent near the house to the north. Look for three large trees.\nThe agent is Senshali Tekar Tavuel [npc=56906] who's located in the northeast corner of the zone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Senshali Tekar Tavuel'\nSenshali Tekar Tavuel's eyes widen as you approach, \"Diabo Sivuela's divination was right, I argued that you wouldn't come, but here you are, ready to help. Be patient mortal. We are expecting an extraction at any moment. Keep your eyes [peeled] for gorongans who are fleeing from the west. They should have been here by now. I'm not sure what is causing them such a delay.'\nYou say, 'peeled'\nSenshali Tekar Tavuel says, 'Quickly \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, the refugees are in need of saving!'\nAt this point, two Centian Xi Datiar [npc=56862] spawn and attack.\n**3\\. Defend yourself from the slavers 0/2 Maiden's Eye**\nDefend yourself from the pursuers!\nKill both slavers. Senshali Tekar Tavuel will help you, along with a few other allied NPCs around.\n**4\\. Speak with Senshali Tekar Tavuel when you are ready to continue 0/1 Maiden's Eye**\nSpeak with Senshali Tekar Tavuel when you are ready to embark.\nYou say, 'Hail, Draues Xean Xirau'\nSenshali Tekar Tavuel approaches you while wiping the blood off of her weapon. 'Well, that was not planned. It appears that was what was holding up the slaves. I wonder who else made it...' Just as Senshali Tekar Tavuel ponders this, two gorongan slaves peer out from behind the trees, scared but unharmed. 'They must have snuck here during the chaos. Only two left? It is a good thing we have you here with us today, mortal. Please, let us begin our escape.'\nTwo newly freed slaves [npc=56863] spawn and start heading south. Follow them.\n**5\\. Defend yourself from the patrollers! 0/2 Maiden's Eye**\nDefend yourself from the scouts!\nTwo patrolling scouts [npc=57167] spawn and attack. Kill them.\n**6\\. Check back in with Senshali Tekar Tavuel 0/1 Maiden's Eye**\nSenshali Tekar Tavuel examines the bodies of the fallen tegi for a moment before speaking to you, 'This is how it has been since Ka Vethan has been restored. The reclamation officers here are willing to go through all of this just to maintain order here in the Maiden's Eye. We must be on high alert, as they like to use tegi as scouts. Surely there will be alarms when these two do not report back soon.' Senshali Tekar Tavuel looks south and says, 'Let us continue.'\n**7\\. Ensure the refugees get to the safety of the camp.**\nContinue to the camp.\n**8\\. Defend yourself from the slave patrollers! 0/2 Maiden's Eye**\nDefend yourself from yet another ambush!\nOnce again, two Centian Xi Datiar attack. Kill them.\n**9\\. Continue to the camp.**\nContinue your journey. The camp is ahead.\nKeep heading south until you reach the southeast camp.\n**10\\. Speak with Diabo Sivuela about what has transpired 0/1 Maiden's Eye**\nThe long trek is over. The survivors are safe and taken care of at the camp. Return to Diabo Sivuela.\nDiabo Sivuela says, 'The operation wasn't a full success, but you did show that you can be trusted within this camp. Understand mortal, you are only a visitor here, more so than we are. Forgetting your place will not bode well for your future here on Luclin. I suggest you hold strong to that knowledge. I've got my eye on you, but if you wish to continue your efforts here today, speak with Torgarath Rulour Thox [npc=56886] and they will find more work for you to do.\"'\nYou have received a replay timer for 'Threading the Loop': 0d:0h:15m remaining.\nYou have gained the trust of Diabo Sivuela, what you will do with that trust is up to you.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\nMoney for your level\nExperience for your level\n**Submitted by:** Drewie",
